The checkpointed two-stage reverse-mode algorithm in src/darkmagic/engine.py
and the metasmoothness diagnostic are adapted from Bergson MAGIC and the local
MagicLens implementation of Bergson at commit 83c1412. Copyright (c) 2025
EleutherAI. Its MIT license is reproduced in licenses/bergson-MIT.txt.
The adapter/optimizer implementation here is owned by DarkMagic; Bergson is not
a runtime dependency and is not included as a submodule.

src/darkmagic/labels.py adapts the Jacobian estimator in
https://github.com/anthropics/jacobian-lens at
581d398613e5602a5af361e1c34d3a92ea82ba8e.
Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC. Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
It retains the reference estimator's position reduction. jacobian-lens is not
a runtime dependency and is not included as a submodule.

The paired data originates in the Phantom Transfer teacher datasets and the
GhostBusters experiment cohorts. Generated length-control datasets and cached
feature labels are attributed separately in data/README.md and data/manifest.json.
Base-model/SAE weights are not redistributed in the code repository. The private
artifact dataset separately retains the final experiment LoRA adapters. Downloading them is subject to their
upstream licenses and, where applicable, Hugging Face access requirements.

The shifted-sum convolution in src/darkmagic/qwen.py is adapted from the local
MagicLens fast_depthwise_conv implementation. It is included as an owned module
with the original parameter names, without process-wide monkeypatching. The
figure renderers adapt the author's GhostBusters plotting scripts; source
artifact paths and hashes are retained in the dataset manifest.
